      "writtenOn": "2024-05-21T10:54:27Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The SMCCC defines `res` as a 64-bit value so casting is a violation of the spec.\n\nInside the `if cfg!`, we do so (\"`res as u32`\") because we know that it is somewhat fine to ignore the 32 MSBs but that is not always true and the path without the workaround must use the 64-bit value as-is to correctly support any valid error code.",
      "parentUuid": "629d46d1_8200a1e7",
